course: dictionary
lesson: 6223
title: Mitt, glove or joke
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mitt is a glove with one part for the thumb and one big part for all four fingers together. The context often tells you which kind of mitt is meant. «Most kitchen accidents happen in a moment, so good habits matter more than luck: turn pot handles in, use dry oven mitts, carry knives pointing down and wipe up spills at once.» Kitchen and hot pans tell you the mitts are for protecting your hands.
explain: «Oven mitts must be dry, because heat passes quickly through a wet cloth and can burn your hand.» The clues are heat, wet cloth and burn. So a mitt protects your hand from heat. If the mitt gets wet, the heat gets through, so the mitt is no longer safe.
explain: Mitt can have other meanings too. A baseball mitt is for catching the ball, so the sport words tell you what it is. Mitts can also be a jokey word for hands. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Keep your mitts off the cake!» means keep your hands off the cake, so mitts means hands here.
fact: A mitt is a glove with one part for the thumb and one part for all four fingers together.
fact: Mitten means the same as mitt in its first meaning.
fact: «Oven mitt» means a thick, padded glove used to hold hot pans and trays.
fact: «Baseball mitt» means a large leather glove for catching the ball.
fact: «Keep your mitts off» means do not touch, and mitts is a jokey word for hands.
exercise: «Oven mitts must be dry, because heat passes quickly through a wet cloth and can burn your hand.» Why must oven mitts be dry? | Wet cloth is heavier to carry | Wet cloth lets heat through and can burn your hand | Dry cloth is cheaper to buy | *Wet mitts look untidy
exercise: A baseball player wears a mitt on one hand. What is the mitt for? | To keep the feet warm in the snow | *To catch the ball | To hit the ball far | To cook dinner in the oven
exercise: Mum says, «Keep your mitts off the cake!» What does mitts mean here? | Feet | Oven cloths | Gloves for the snow | *Hands
test: «Use dry oven mitts to take hot trays out of the oven.» What are oven mitts for? | Covering the eyes | Keeping your feet warm | Catching a ball | *Holding hot pans and trays safely
test: Ella says, «A mitt has a part for the thumb and one part for the four fingers.» What is she describing? | A hat | *A glove, also called a mitten | A scarf | A sock
exam: «Most kitchen accidents happen in a moment, so good habits matter more than luck.» What is the author's main point? | Kitchens are dangerous places, so never go in | *Good habits, such as using dry oven mitts, help stop kitchen accidents | Hot pans should be carried by hand without gloves | Luck is the only way to stay safe in the kitchen
